Aerie-Purpose: Put the "Close a pinned tab" row in the Sidebar section of Settings, let the settings page write its pref, and give the page its strings.
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/browser/resources/settings (appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.ts, appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts, BUILD.gn), chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings (settings_localized_strings_provider.cc), chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private (prefs_util.cc)
Aerie-Kind: hook

Issue #180. The row, settings-aerie-pinned-close-row, is a Lit element in the overlay
(chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/aerie_pinned_close_row.*). It is a
settings-dropdown-menu on the pref aerie.tabs.pinned_close (a string, registered by
components/aerie_tab_model/tab_model_prefs.cc), with the options reset-sleep-switch (default), sleep and close.
The pref name is a string literal in the settings_private allowlist, as for the other Aerie prefs, and a test
compares it with aerie_tab_model::kPinnedClose. Its strings are in the overlay's aerie_sidebar_strings.grdp,
which patches/sidebar/0022 includes in generated_resources.grd; this patch hands them to the page. The element
sits in the "Sidebar" section, under the sleep row of patches/sidebar/0035.

--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/api/settings_private/prefs_util.cc
@@ -488,6 +488,9 @@
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.archive_after"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
   (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.sleep_after_minutes"] =
       settings_api::PrefType::kNumber;
+  // Aerie: what Ctrl+W does on a pinned tab (issue #180). The name is
+  // aerie_tab_model::kPinnedClose; a test compares the two.
+  (*s_allowlist)["aerie.tabs.pinned_close"] = settings_api::PrefType::kString;
   // Aerie: the sidebar's width and shown state (issue #177). The names are
   // aerie_sidebar::kWidthPref and kVisiblePref; a test compares them. The
   // layout pref is not here until issue #186 builds the second layout.
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/appearance_page/appearance_layout_page.html.ts
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
   return html`<!--_html_template_start_-->
 <settings-section page-title="$i18n{aerieSidebarPageTitle}">
   <settings-aerie-sleep-row></settings-aerie-sleep-row>
+  <settings-aerie-pinned-close-row></settings-aerie-pinned-close-row>
 </settings-section>
 <!--_html_template_end_-->`;
